title: Panels and the game's own Esc
intro: A script can have Esc before the game menu does, a press a panel uses doesn't reach the game too, a menu bar button works over a letter that pauses the game, and a fly-out closes when you click away.

project: Empty | Panels and Esc

chapter: A tool that has Esc first | ClaimsBack
write: Scripts/BuildTool.cs | panel-input/BuildTool.cs
code: Assets/Scripts/BuildTool.cs | BuildTool.cs
say: A builder's tool. While it's in hand, ClaimsBack is true: Esc is the script's, to put the tool down, before it's the game menu's.
hidecode
deselect
create: Text
rename: Tool
set: Transform.Position = 0, 2, 0
add: BuildTool
deselect
create: Panel
rename: Game Menu
explain: field:Panel.OpenOn | Open On | The game menu opens on Pause: Esc, P or Start.
set: Panel.OpenOn = Pause
create: Button
rename: Quit
set: Button.Action = Quit

chapter: Play | Esc puts the tool down, then opens the menu
play
wait: 1
expectvalue: Tool.BuildTool.Held = true
tap: Escape
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Tool.BuildTool.Held = false
expectvalue: Game Menu.Panel.Open = false
say: The first Esc put the tool down, and the menu waited.
tap: Escape
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Game Menu.Panel.Open = true
say: With nothing in hand, the next Esc opens the game menu.
tap: Escape
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Game Menu.Panel.Open = false
expectvalue: Tool.BuildTool.EscSeen = 1
say: And Esc closes it again. The script saw only the first Esc: the presses the menu used, opening and closing it, didn't reach the game too.
stop

chapter: A menu bar over a letter | Over Panels
deselect
create: Panel
rename: Letter
set: Panel.Open = true
create: Text
set: Text.Value = Welcome to the factory. Read this before you build.
deselect
create: Button
rename: Game
set: Transform.Position = -6, 4, 0
set: Button.Action = OpenPanel
set: Button.Panel = Game Menu
set: Button.Shortcut = F10
explain: field:Button.OverPanels | Over Panels | Over Panels keeps the menu bar's Game button working while a panel it isn't on is open, even one that pauses the game.
set: Button.OverPanels = true
play
wait: 1
expectvalue: Letter.Panel.Open = true
tap: F10
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Game Menu.Panel.Open = true
expectvalue: Letter.Panel.Open = true
say: The game opens on the letter, and F10 opens the game menu over it.
tap: Escape
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Game Menu.Panel.Open = false
expectvalue: Letter.Panel.Open = true
say: Closing the game menu leaves the letter open, where it was.
stop
chapter: A fly-out | Popup
select: Letter
set: Panel.Open = false
deselect
create: Panel
rename: Contracts
deselect
create: Panel
rename: Fly Out
set: Sprite.Size = 4, 2.5
set: Panel.PauseGame = false
explain: field:Panel.Popup | Popup | A pop-up closes as soon as the player clicks anywhere off it, and that click does nothing else.
set: Panel.Popup = true
create: Button
rename: Belt
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0.6, 0
select: Fly Out
create: Button
rename: Open Contracts
set: Transform.Position = 0, -0.6, 0
set: Button.Action = OpenPanel
set: Button.Panel = Contracts
deselect
create: Button
rename: Palette
set: Transform.Position = -6, -3, 0
set: Button.Action = OpenPanel
set: Button.Panel = Fly Out
play
wait: 1
gameclick: Palette
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Fly Out.Panel.Open = true
say: The palette's icon opens its fly-out.
gameclick: 6, 3
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Fly Out.Panel.Open = false
say: A click off it closes it, and goes no further: a builder's tool wouldn't lay anything there.
gameclick: Palette
wait: 0.5
gameclick: Open Contracts
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Contracts.Panel.Open = true
expectvalue: Fly Out.Panel.Open = false
say: Picking something on it closes it once the pick is done. This one opened the contracts window in the fly-out's place.
tap: Escape
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Contracts.Panel.Open = false
say: So closing the window shows nothing left underneath.
stop
